                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m(i(x),x) = e
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+homomorphism"} group homomorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
                in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            Note that it is not necessary to draw explicit trees; these can be recovered from the succinct equations like
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m(m(x,y),z) = m(x,m(y,z))
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The variety of
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoids"} monoids
                is given by a subtheory of the theory of groups. It has only the operations
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ,
                      %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m,e
                and the axioms
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ass"} (1)
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:runit"} (2)
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:lunit"} (3)
            %li
              %p
                There is no variety of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cancellative+monoid"}> cancellative monoid
                    s
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = y
                follows from the equation
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi m
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi z
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi m
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi y
                        %mo ,
                        %mi z
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m(x,z) = m(y,z)
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi m
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi z
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi m
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi y
                        %mo ,
                        %mi z
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊢
                        %mi x
                        %mo =
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m(x,z) = m(y,z) \vdash x = y
            %li
              %p
                The variety of
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
                is given by a supertheory of the theory of groups. In addition to the operations and axioms of the variety of groups, it has an additional axiom, the commutative law:
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi m
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi m
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi y
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m(x,y) = m(y,x)
            %li
              %p
                The variety of (associative unital)
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rings"} rings
                has five operations
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi z
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %mi m
                        %mo ,
                        %mi e
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,z,n,m,e
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2,0,2,0,1
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi z
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,z,n
                in place of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi m
                        %mo ,
                        %mi e
                        %mo ,
                        %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m,e,i
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ,
                      %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m,e
                as before). The remaining two axioms are:
              %ul
                %li
                  left distributive law:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi m
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi y
                          %mo ,
                          %mi z
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi m
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi m
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi z
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m(x,a(y,z)) = a(m(x,y),m(x,z))
                %li
                  right distributive law:
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi m
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi z
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi m
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi z
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi m
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi y
                          %mo ,
                          %mi z
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m(a(x,y),z) = a(m(x,z),m(y,z))
            %li
              %p
                There is no variety or quasivariety of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fields"} fields
            %li
              %p
                The variety of (real)
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
                has infinitely many operations and axioms (so is not finitary). First, there are operations
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi z
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,z,n
                with the arities and axioms of an abelian group (as with rings). In addition, there is one operation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi m
                        %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_r
                of arity
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                for each
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real number
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
              %ul
                %li
                  left distributive law: for each real number
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi r
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi m
                            %mi r
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi m
                            %mi r
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi m
                            %mi r
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_r(a(x,y)) = a(m_r(x),m_r(y))
                %li
                  right distributive law: for each real number
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
                  and real number
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi m
                          %mrow
                            %mi r
                            %mo +
                            %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi m
                          %mi r
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi m
                          %mi r
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_{r+s}(x) = a(m_r(x),m_r(y))
                  (where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                        %mo +
                        %mi s
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r + s
                  is the sum of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
                  as real numbers),
                %li
                  associative law: for each real number
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
                  and real number
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi m
                          %mrow
                            %mi r
                            %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi m
                          %mi r
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi m
                          %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_{r s}(x) = m_r(m_s(x))
                  (where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                        %mi s
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r s
                  is the product of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
                  as real numbers),
                %li
                  unit law:
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi m
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_1(x) = x
                  (where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                  the real number
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1"} 1
            %li
              %p
                There is a similar variety of vector spaces over any given
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
                over arbitrary
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+rings"} commutative rings
                either. However, there is a
                %em sorted
                variety of modules over arbitrary rings, with two types, one for the ring and one for the module. Even though this variety includes the non-finitary variety of real vector spaces, it is itself a finitary sorted variety.
          %h2#as_algebraic_theories As algebraic theories
          %p
            A variety of algebras is one way to look at an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+theory"} algebraic theory
          %p
            As a
            = succeed "al" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logic"} logic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+logic"} cartesian logic
            (although one might want to use something stronger, such as full classical or intuitionistic predicate logic with equality). We use one function symbol (of matching arity) for each operation, and each axiom in the variety becomes an axiom in the logic, a universally quantified equation. Then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/models"} models
            of this logical theory are the same as the algebras in the variety.
          %p
            As a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory"} Lawvere theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            whose objects are of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^n
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            a natural number. The morphisms of the category are those which are necessary to make
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^n
            the
            = succeed "-fold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is freely generated by these as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sketch"} sketch
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            are the same as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product-preserving+functor"} product-preserving
            functors from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small
            (and hence
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^n
            may be thought of as a Lawvere theory and defines an untyped variety of algebras, with operation for each morphism to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and one axiom for each commutative diagram. (This can all be generalised to sorted varieties as well.)
          %p
            A variety of algebras can be seen as a cartesian version of a (typed or untyped)
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
          %p
            A variety of algebras is traditionally identified with its category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            of models in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            (or even with simply the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
            of objects of this category), but it then becomes unclear what an algebra in the variety would be in some other category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is always an
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+category"} algebraic category
          %h2#free_algebras Free algebras
          %p
            Given a variety
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            (such as
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^V
            be the category of algebras in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\colon C^V \to C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocomplete+category"} cocomplete
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/W-pretopos"} pretopos
            (or if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is just a
            = succeed "-pretopos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is finitary), then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            has a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+functor"} free functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon C \to C^V
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+adjunction"} monadic
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+of+a+monad"} modules/algebras
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \circ F
          %p
            Given an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(A)
            as follows. First, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(A)
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inductive+type"} inductive type
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            given by the signature of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+algebra"} initial algebra
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctor"} endofunctor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi o
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %mo #
                        %mi o
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \mapsto \sum_o A^{\#o}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi o
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} o
            ranges over the operations of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo #
                  %mi o
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \#o
            is the arity of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi o
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} o
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation"} relation
            on
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(A)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            of these is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(A)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a set, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(A)
            consists precisely of the words (defined as trees above) with variables from
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            The
            %strong word problem
            for a variety
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            consists of deciding, whenever
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(A)
            are equal in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(A)
          %ul
            %li
              trivial for
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+algebras"} Boolean algebras
            %li
              impossible for
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+algebras"} Heyting algebras
            %li
              nontrivial but possible for
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattices"} lattices
          %p even though each of these is a supertheory of the next.
          %h2#literature Literature
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ji%C5%99%C3%AD+Ad%C3%A1mek"}> Jiří Adámek
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere"} F.W. Lawvere
              = succeed "," do
                %em On the duality between varieties and algebraic theories
              = succeed ":1," do
                %strong 49
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s000120300002"} doi
          .footnotes
            %hr/
            %ol
              %li#fn:1
                %p
                  For a finitary signature, we may without loss of generality use the set
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi V
                          %mo ≔
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mn 2
                          %mo ,
                          %mi …
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \coloneqq \{x_0, x_1, x_2, \ldots\}
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
                  %a{:href => "#fnref:1", :rev => "footnote"} ↩
